{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"304a1baa-b122-42fc-a8d5-e28032259920","status":"SUCCESS","response":"Applied the fixes across [schema.py](file:///C:/Users/jayde/AppData/Local/Temp/ai_lab_disposable_workspaces/live_BENCH-011_24720_1795489239808_icm_staged/schema.py), [upcaster.py](file:///C:/Users/jayde/AppData/Local/Temp/ai_lab_disposable_workspaces/live_BENCH-011_24720_1795489239808_icm_staged/upcaster.py), [store.py](file:///C:/Users/jayde/AppData/Local/Temp/ai_lab_disposable_workspaces/live_BENCH-011_24720_1795489239808_icm_staged/store.py), and [projector.py](file:///C:/Users/jayde/AppData/Local/Temp/ai_lab_disposable_workspaces/live_BENCH-011_24720_1795489239808_icm_staged/projector.py):\n\n- `schema.py` (`Event.__post_init__`): Added strict `schema_version` validation (`type(self.schema_version) is int` and in `(1, 2, 3)`).\n- `upcaster.py` (`upcast`): Replaced `elif` with sequential `if` blocks so v1 chains through v2 to v3, and raised `ValueError` when `\"amount\"` is missing from a v1 payload.\n- `store.py` (`EventStore.append`, `EventStore.read`): Enforced `expected_version != current`, deep-copied and validated every event before mutating `_streams`, and returned deep copies from `append` and `read`.\n- `projector.py` (`replay`): Passed `after_version=version` to `store.read` so snapshot replay only processes the tail after the snapshot version.\n\nVerified with `python -m pytest -q --tb=short` (`1 passed in 0.02s`).\n","duration_seconds":23.402949800000002,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":35919,"output_tokens":2174,"thinking_tokens":100,"cache_read_tokens":103674,"total_tokens":38093}}}
